::PC_U02_L04_Q_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U02_L04_Q_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.TR.1
Question:
Convert 30 degrees to radians. Which setup shows the correct conversion process?
{
~A. 30 degrees multiplied by 180/pi #This choice uses a related idea but does not complete the required reasoning for the stated standard.
~B. 30 degrees divided by 180pi #This choice reflects a common misconception or an incomplete step.
=C. 30 degrees multiplied by pi/180 #Correct. This answer follows the lesson concept and connects the result to the stated standard.
~D. 30 degrees plus pi/180 #This choice does not match the conditions in the question.
}

